 ],
 "title": "Regulation of Gene Expression and Pathways in Fungi and Bacteria",
 "summary": "This cluster is about the regulation of gene expression and pathways in fungi and bacteria. Cryptococcus neoformans expresses Kex2p, a process or phenotype, and interacts with influenza virus. The CRP regulon regulates adenylate cyclase, crr, and cyaA genes in E. coli K-12 MG1655. BPMs identifies LocalCut and trims itself to ILP. GIDEON, a method or tool, funded by the National Institute of General Medical Sciences, identifies BPMs and outperforms LocalCut. cAMP binds to CRP and produces adenylate cyclase. ERG11 and ERG3 are upregulated by KTZ. M. pachydermatis is added to KTZ. The cluster also involves ALE experiments, ALEdb, and mutations in E. coli K-12 MG1655.",
